{/*
  The interactive core-flow diagram — home band 2. The first member of the §5 interactive
  semantic-HTML contract class (docs/design/docs-site-visual-blueprint.md §5): one responsive
  semantic-HTML/CSS representation of the plan-driven spine (seven stages, review loops),
  three independent collapsed-by-default satellite disclosures (gist authoring, objective
  authoring, the docs/learned cache with its harvest + dreaming curation loops), and labeled
  dashed feeds. No <svg> anywhere: all semantics live in source order and visible text;
  connectors are CSS-generated decorative glyphs/rules in the accessibility-neutral
  `content: "…" / ""` form. Colors come only from existing --perk-* / --sl-color-* custom
  properties on §9-verified pairs; every font-size is declared in px and >= 16.

  Layout is container-keyed on the figure's inline size (compositions.css makes
  figure.perk-diagram an inline-size container): vertical spine + stacked satellites by
  default (and in no-container-query browsers); from 640px the spine becomes a horizontal
  wrapping row whose stages stack their loop/condition annotations under the chips; from
  960px the satellites take a three-up row and the compacted spine reads as a single
  horizontal row at the 1280/1600 acceptance widths (wrapping stays as the narrow-container
  safety — the no-overflow invariant outranks single-line rendering). No viewport media query.

  No-JS/print strategy: the three <details> ship `open` in source, so the unenhanced page
  (and the static a11y gate, which never runs scripts) is content-complete. The processed
  module script below mounts src/core-flow-controller.mjs, which removes `open` on enhance,
  re-opens on `beforeprint`/restores on `afterprint`, and drives the 9 supplementary tooltips
  (7 stage chips + the 2 cache loops — hover/focus intent, tap pinning on hover-incapable
  devices, a document-level Escape dismiss latch, one visible at a time). Tooltips stay
  hoverable (SC 1.4.13): the controller holds hover intent for the tooltip itself and the
  ::after hit-area bridges the 8px gap. Tooltip copy is supplementary color only; every
  tooltip is the sibling of its real <button> trigger inside the same position:relative
  .tip-wrap, with aria-describedby always pointing at it.

  `▸ implement` is shown as an example in-flight stage (visually-hidden `(current)` carries
  the state accessibly); review loops name their shipped surfaces truthfully — human review
  is the universal plan/objective gate, the agent draft-review wave is an optional
  browser-door assist, gist authoring is human-review only.
*/}

<figure class="perk-diagram perk-core-flow" data-core-flow>
  <ol class="flow-spine">
    <li class="stage">
      <span class="tip-wrap">
        <button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-plan">
          <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">○</span> plan
        </button>
        <span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-plan" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>
          A read-only session explores the repo and authors a bounded plan; a human review
          gates it before save — on the browser review door an agent draft-review wave
          assists.
        </span>
      </span>
      <span class="loop"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> human review · optional agent wave</span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage">
      <span class="tip-wrap">
        <button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-save">
          <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">○</span> save
        </button>
        <span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-save" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>
          The approved plan is persisted as a durable issue — the canonical artifact the rest
          of the workflow consumes.
        </span>
      </span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage current">
      <span class="tip-wrap">
        <button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-implement">
          <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">▸</span> implement<span class="visually-hidden"> (current)</span>
        </button>
        <span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-implement" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>
          A worktree session executes the saved plan and runs the repo's CI checks before
          submitting.
        </span>
      </span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage">
      <span class="tip-wrap">
        <button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-submit">
          <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">○</span> submit
        </button>
        <span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-submit" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>
          The change goes up as a pull request for human review.
        </span>
      </span>
      <span class="loop"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> human PR review</span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage conditional">
      <span class="tip-wrap">
        <button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-address">
          <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">◇</span> address
        </button>
        <span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-address" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>
          Review feedback is classified and resolved — this stage runs only when review asks.
        </span>
      </span>
      <span class="condition">(if review asks)</span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage">
      <span class="tip-wrap">
        <button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-land">
          <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">○</span> land
        </button>
        <span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-land" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>
          The approved pull request merges; objective nodes advance and reconcile
          automatically.
        </span>
      </span>
    </li>
    <li class="stage">
      <span class="tip-wrap">
        <button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-learn">
          <span class="glyph" aria-hidden="true">○</span> learn
        </button>
        <span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-learn" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>
          Durable learnings from the session are captured into learn issues for later
          consolidation.
        </span>
      </span>
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="satellites">
    <details open data-core-flow-disclosure>
      <summary>
        <span class="sat-label">gist authoring</span> <span class="sat-hint">problem statements — plan → save</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="sat-body">
        <p class="mini-flow">
          <span class="mini-stage">plan</span><span class="mini-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="mini-stage">save</span>
          <span class="loop"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> human review</span>
        </p>
        <ul class="feeds">
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> objective plan — seeds an objective</li>
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> spine plan — seeds a plan</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details open data-core-flow-disclosure>
      <summary>
        <span class="sat-label">objective authoring</span> <span class="sat-hint">plans of plans — plan → save</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="sat-body">
        <p class="mini-flow">
          <span class="mini-stage">plan</span><span class="mini-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="mini-stage">save</span>
          <span class="loop"><span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> human review · optional agent wave</span>
        </p>
        <ul class="feeds">
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> spine plan — each node emits a bounded plan</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details open data-core-flow-disclosure>
      <summary>
        <span class="sat-label">docs/learned</span> <span class="sat-hint">the durable learned-docs cache</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="sat-body">
        <div class="cache">
          <span class="tip-wrap">
            <button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-harvest">
              <span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> harvest → objective authoring
            </button>
            <span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-harvest" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>
              Harvest mines docs/learned for improvement opportunities and authors one
              bounded objective — an objective factory, never a direct plan.
            </span>
          </span>
          <span class="tip-wrap">
            <button type="button" data-core-flow-tip aria-describedby="perk-core-flow-tip-dreaming">
              <span aria-hidden="true">↻</span> dreaming — corpus self-curation
            </button>
            <span role="tooltip" id="perk-core-flow-tip-dreaming" hidden data-core-flow-tooltip>
              Dreaming reads the learned corpus as a whole and authors a reviewed curation
              objective — pruning and consolidating perk's memory.
            </span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <ul class="feeds">
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> spine plan — ambient learned context</li>
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> objective plan — ambient learned context</li>
          <li class="feed"><span class="feed-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> gist plan — ambient learned context</li>
          <li class="feed">spine learn <span aria-hidden="true">⇢</span> docs/learned — mediated: /learn captures learn issues; perk learn docs folds them into the corpus</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</figure>

<style>
  /* --- Spine: vertical by default (also the no-container-query rendering) ----------------- */
  .flow-spine {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    row-gap: 8px;
  }

  .stage {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    column-gap: 12px;
    row-gap: 4px;
  }

  /* Decorative CSS-generated connectors (the accessibility-neutral alt form): ↓/→ solid
     transitions, ⇣/⇢ the dashed conditional transition into address. */
  .stage + .stage::before {
    content: "↓" / "";
    inline-size: 100%;
    padding-inline-start: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--perk-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .stage + .stage.conditional::before {
    content: "⇣" / "";
  }

  .stage button[data-core-flow-tip] {
    background: var(--perk-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-radius: var(--perk-radius-control);
    padding: 5px 12px;
    color: var(--perk-text);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.4;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .stage.current button[data-core-flow-tip] {
    border: 2px solid var(--perk-accent);
    padding: 4px 11px;
    color: var(--perk-accent);
  }

  .glyph {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
  }
  .stage.current .glyph {
    color: var(--perk-accent);
  }

  .loop {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .condition {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font), sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .visually-hidden {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    margin: -1px;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* --- Satellites: stacked full-width by default ------------------------------------------ */
  .satellites {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    margin-block-start: 28px;
  }

  .satellites details {
    background: var(--perk-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-radius: var(--perk-radius-card);
  }

  .satellites summary {
    padding: 12px 16px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .sat-label {
    color: var(--perk-text);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .sat-hint {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font), sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .sat-body {
    padding: 2px 16px 16px;
  }

  .mini-flow {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    column-gap: 8px;
    row-gap: 6px;
    color: var(--perk-text);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .mini-stage {
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-radius: var(--perk-radius-control);
    padding: 2px 8px;
  }

  .mini-arrow {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
  }

  /* The docs/learned durable-cache cylinder (CSS-shaped: elliptical rim over a rounded-base
     body; decorative geometry only — the loop labels carry the semantics). */
  .cache {
    position: relative;
    margin-block: 16px 14px;
    padding: 20px 14px 14px;
    background: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-block-start: none;
    border-radius: 0 0 50% 50% / 0 0 12px 12px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    row-gap: 6px;
  }
  .cache::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: -1px;
    inset-block-start: -9px;
    block-size: 18px;
    background: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .cache .tip-wrap button {
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 2px 4px;
    text-align: start;
    color: var(--perk-text);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .feeds {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    row-gap: 7px;
  }

  /* Labeled feeds: the dashed-rule treatment is decoration; the label is the semantics.
     The rule takes the §5 legend row's bound muted token, like the feed text. */
  .feed {
    border-block-start: 1px dashed var(--perk-muted);
    padding-block-start: 7px;
    color: var(--perk-muted);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono), monospace;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .feed-glyph {
    color: var(--perk-muted);
  }

  /* --- Supplementary tooltips (colocated siblings of their triggers) ---------------------- */
  .tip-wrap {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
  }

  [data-core-flow-tooltip] {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: calc(100% + 8px);
    left: 50%;
    transform: translateX(-50%);
    width: max-content;
    max-width: min(36ch, calc(100cqw - 16px));
    padding: 8px 10px;
    background: var(--perk-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--perk-border);
    border-radius: var(--perk-radius-control);
    color: var(--perk-text);
    font-family: var(--sl-font), sans-serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.4;
    text-align: start;
    z-index: 3;
  }
  /* SC 1.4.13 hoverable: a hit-area bridge over the 8px gap below the tooltip, so the
     pointer can cross from the trigger onto the tooltip without passing dead space (the
     controller holds hover intent for the tooltip too). Oversized by 4px into both boxes
     so sub-pixel rounding can never open a dead strip. Decorative-empty, hit-test only. */
  [data-core-flow-tooltip]::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: 0;
    inset-block-end: -12px;
    block-size: 16px;
  }

  [data-core-flow-tooltip][data-align="start"] {
    left: 0;
    transform: none;
  }
  [data-core-flow-tooltip][data-align="end"] {
    left: auto;
    right: 0;
    transform: none;
  }
  [data-core-flow-tooltip][hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  /* --- Container flips: horizontal spine from 640px, three-up satellites from 960px ------- */
  @container (min-width: 640px) {
    .flow-spine {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      column-gap: 10px;
      row-gap: 16px;
    }
    /* Each stage compacts into a chip row with its loop/condition annotation stacked
       beneath, so the chip strip reads as one instrument row (the connector stays centered
       on the chip row). */
    .stage {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto auto;
      column-gap: 10px;
      row-gap: 4px;
      align-items: center;
    }
    .stage + .stage::before {
      content: "→" / "";
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 1;
      inline-size: auto;
      padding-inline-start: 0;
    }
    .stage + .stage.conditional::before {
      content: "⇢" / "";
    }
    .stage .tip-wrap {
      grid-column: 2;
      grid-row: 1;
      justify-self: start;
    }
    .stage .loop,
    .stage .condition {
      grid-column: 2;
      grid-row: 2;
      justify-self: start;
      max-width: 24ch;
    }
  }

  @container (min-width: 960px) {
    /* The wide-spine arm: the compacted stages read as a single horizontal row at the
       1280/1600 acceptance widths; wrapping remains solely as the narrow-container safety
       (the §6 no-overflow invariant outranks single-line rendering). */
    .flow-spine {
      column-gap: 8px;
    }
    .stage {
      column-gap: 8px;
    }
    .stage .loop,
    .stage .condition {
      max-width: 20ch;
    }
    .satellites {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 16px;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // The site's first (and only) repo-owned client script: mount the extracted, unit-tested
  // interaction controller on every core-flow figure. Unenhanced pages (no JS, print, the
  // static a11y gate) are content-complete from source — enhancement only collapses the
  // satellites and adds the supplementary tooltips.
  import { enhanceCoreFlow } from "../core-flow-controller.mjs";

  for (const root of document.querySelectorAll("[data-core-flow]")) {
    enhanceCoreFlow(root);
  }
</script>
